---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

/* Sourced from docs/COMPARISON.md, which is itself sourced from a survey of
 * Restreamer's issue trackers.
 *
 * Every row here is a capability polyemesis has and the others do not, stated
 * as a fact a reader can check against their own install rather than as a
 * claim. docs/COMPARISON.md carries the full picture including where the other
 * tools lead, for anyone who wants it. */

/* [capability, polyemesis, Restreamer, restream.io]
 *
 * polyemesis is a column in the data rather than a hardcoded "Yes" in the
 * markup. It was the latter for one commit, which works exactly until somebody
 * adds a row this project does not win — and then the table asserts something
 * false while looking maintained. */
const wins = [
  ["Per-destination audio mix from one multitrack ingest", "Yes", "No", "No"],
  ["Channel-level mix matrix with per-cell gain", "Yes", "No", "No"],
  ["Per-destination loudness target, measured after routing", "Yes", "No", "No"],
  ["Multitrack archive — every ingest track preserved, stream-copied", "Yes", "No", "No"],
  ["Per-track stems as 24-bit WAV or FLAC, segment-aligned", "Yes", "No", "No"],
  ["Track annotations — what each incoming track actually is", "Yes", "No", "No"],
  ["Typed SRT rejections — the publisher is told why it was refused", "Yes", "No", "n/a"],
  ["Runs on hardware you control, no per-destination pricing", "Yes", "Yes", "No"],
];

---

<Base
  title="polyemesis vs Restreamer vs restream.io — self-hosted restreaming compared"
  description="A self-hosted Restreamer and restream.io alternative. Per-destination audio from one multitrack ingest is the thing neither of them does — see the capability table."
  path="/comparison"
>
  <section class="wrap py-16 sm:py-20">
    <p class="eyebrow">Comparison</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-balance text-4xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-5xl">
      The audio is the difference.
    </h1>

    {/* Primary, not amber. This is the thesis of the whole page, and amber is
        reserved for things that carry an operational signal. */}
    <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl rounded-token border-l-2 border-primary bg-surface/60 py-4 pl-5 pr-4">
      <p class="text-pretty leading-relaxed text-fg">
        <strong>polyemesis is built for one case, completely:</strong>
        <em>this</em> platform gets the clean mix, <em>that</em> one gets the
        full mix — from a single upload and a single video encode, with the
        picture never re-encoded to do it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-pretty leading-relaxed text-muted">
        That is the case the whole product is arranged around: the routing
        matrix, the per-destination loudness targets, the multitrack archive and
        the stems all exist because the audio is the hard part and everything
        else in this space treats it as one stereo pair.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap pb-16" data-reveal>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium">What polyemesis has that neither has</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-token border border-line">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[46rem] border-collapse text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-surface">
          <tr class="border-b border-line">
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-medium">Capability</th>
            {/* polyemesis first, and in the primary colour. The table used to
                list only the other two and leave the reader to infer who did
                these things from a column of "No" — which reads as a table
                ABOUT the competitors. The subject of a comparison should be in
                it. */}
            <th scope="col" class="w-32 px-4 py-3 text-center font-medium text-primary">polyemesis</th>
            <th scope="col" class="w-32 px-4 py-3 text-center font-medium">Restreamer</th>
            <th scope="col" class="w-32 px-4 py-3 text-center font-medium">restream.io</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            wins.map(([cap, poly, a, b]) => (
              <tr class="border-b border-line/60 last:border-0">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-fg">{cap}</td>
                <td class:list={[
                  "px-4 py-3 text-center font-mono text-xs",
                  poly === "Yes" ? "text-live" : "text-subtle",
                ]}>{poly}</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-center font-mono text-xs text-subtle">{a}</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-center font-mono text-xs text-subtle">{b}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-subtle">
      The multitrack ask is not hypothetical. “Multiple audio tracks for Twitch”
      is an open request on Restreamer's own tracker — users asking it for the
      thing polyemesis was built to be.
    </p>
  </section>


  <section class="wrap py-20 text-center" data-reveal>
    <h2 class="text-balance text-3xl font-medium">Still the right problem?</h2>
    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
      <a href="/download" class="btn btn-primary">Install it</a>
      <a href="/#matrix" class="btn btn-ghost">Try the routing matrix</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
